			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4076561">
									

<p>This absolutely shines for sheer writing quality.</p>
<p>Top to bottom. Every single bit of this screams authenticity &#8212; the characters speak and feel like professionals, moreso than can typically be found in an environment of ameturish writing (myself very much included). The handling of Hear No Evil was similarly top notch, and the civilian expert and their concerns came across as wholly realistic.</p>
<p>It's not wildly entertaining. It's a slow-burn mystery surrounding an admittedly dry subject, the handling of which resolves to be quite muted in the end. This however, strengthens the already powerful verisimilitude for me &#8212; though it is a narrative, it feels closer to what an actual SCP file would look like.</p>
<p>+1, and a very well-earned one at that. We need more writing of this calibre.</p>

							</div>

								
					
