														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4076609">
									

<p>So, yeah &#8212; the prose in this is absurdly good; in many aspects, it's <em>intimidatingly</em> good. The density, polish, and clarity with which you write is outstanding throughout &#8212; I also enjoyed the slow-burn mystery of it all. Heck, even the central anomaly is really cool (there's a droning sound in the library and we have no idea where the heck it's coming from &#8212; that's a fantastic low-key hook).</p>
<p>I think the log lags a bit when the characters wax philosophical about Minerva and in a few other spots. There's a number of bits here I think you could trim without losing much of anything, and &#8212; as a minimalist &#8212; I'm contractually obligated to point that out. That being said, even the fatty tissue I'm seeing is still <em>exceedingly</em> well-written. Your prose throughout is a pleasure to read.</p>
<p>Also: I have absolutely no clue if the acoustic science in this article is legitimate, but it almost doesn't matter. You sold it so well that it <em>might as well</em> be.</p>

							</div>

								
					
